een you and your  customers and you may think that you're  doing the right thing by always seeming  professional and on top of things but  really you're making it harder for  people to connect with you look at my  youtube channel as an example if you go  back years you'll find that the advice  that I  given its almost the same advice that I  was giving five years ago right my  opinions haven't changed that much  my advice hasn't changed that much some  of the stories that I'm telling even  those haven't changed is those are still  some of my stories so why am i had so  much success in my channel now compared  to five years ago a big part of it is I  got more personal right if you look at  my videos they were professional  there's me Evan you know talking head  expert but there's no emotion in what  I'm saying I'm not sharing deep personal  stories I'm not sure anything that makes  me feel vulnerable I thought I always  had to be this professional expert who  looked great but now I may be sharing  personal videos I may be sharing my trip  to Disney World I may be sharing me  trying to learn something new and  sucking at it I may be sharing what I'm  doing during the day I'm hearing a lot  more personal content and allowing you  guys to see more of who I am and being  vulnerable like it or not and at first  it's scary at first you feel like you're  opening yourself up to so much criticism  and that people won't like you right you  feel like people will reject you but it  does the exact opposite where what it  does is it opens you up and it allows  people to come in and love you so much  more and feel connected to you and your  business so much more so take a look at  your website take a look at your social  media take a look at all your marketing  are you there is your passion coming  through is your deep story coming  through because the thing that's gonna  separate you from your big competitors  is your story why am I gonna buy from a  small entrepreneur instead of 